  <figure class="deck-notes">
    <figcaption class="deck-ex-plate">Speaker notes · slide 7</figcaption>
    <blockquote>
      <p>Claim: the sources disagree on messaging, and this is the one scope call we need from you. Recommend B.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>The strategy brief scoped messaging out of the MVP. The flows and the service blueprint both assume a coordination step after the seller accepts: a suggested meeting point at the nearest intersection, plus quick replies.</li>
        <li>Why B: without it, an accepted interest has no way to become a pickup, and completion is the number the MVP exists to prove. Quick replies also keep harassment structurally impossible: no free text between people with fewer than three completed exchanges.</li>
        <li>What B doesn't add: open chat, payments, delivery or multi-neighborhood browsing. Those stay out.</li>
        <li>Known design debt: evaluation flagged the pickup screen as overloaded (meeting point, time window and messaging in one view). The fix is progressive disclosure.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Feedback wanted: A or B. Not wanted today: quick-reply wording.</p>
      <p>Source: /strategize, Proposed Scope; /journey, Flows 3 and 4; /blueprint, Decision Documentation; /evaluate, E-11; /fortify, stress test.</p>
      <p>Transition: here's what the evaluation found before anything was built.</p>
    </blockquote>
  </figure>
